# Line endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is common on Windows, and it turned `deploy/entrypoint.sh` into a
# CRLF file in the working tree. The kernel then reads the shebang as `/bin/sh\r`, and the
# container dies at start-up with `exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: no such file or
# directory` — a message that names the file it just failed to run. CI never saw it,
# because Linux runners check out LF. Anything a Linux kernel or shell has to interpret is
# therefore pinned to LF here, whatever the cloner's git is configured to do.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Binary payloads git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webm binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.ico binary
